A||||3||spike||Body pannels out of Wack||||5||
Z||000000||spike||06-27-2000||07:10 PM||||Well as some of you may know I just picked up my Fiero yesterday It's a 85 Fiero SE, Blue Ext., 95500km, Automatic, with a full GT Fastback Body on it. I noticed that many of the body panels didn't line up wright and this was already starting to drive me crazy. I know that the fastback conversion was added so I figured that was the cause of the rear clip and door panels not alingned. The front nose and hood are also out a bit. How easy is it to remove the body panels.<P>Tks. Mike<P> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||coyote||06-28-2000||01:25 PM||||body panels are actually quite easy to remove. its the aero-moulding and the lower facia thats a bit of job. the front quarters have 1 rivet at the lower corner by the door that will have to be drilled out. the rocker cover will have to have the rivets punched out as well. there is 1 rivet on the rear quarter that will have to be punched out. if you remove the molding remember to pull it straight up before pulling out, you have to dis-engage the retaining clips or they will shater. the rest is a combo of 7 and 10 mm bolts.<P>Coyote||||reg||1
Z||000002||fldevel||06-28-2000||02:10 PM|||| body panels can be ajusted about 1/8 of an inch (give or take) either way if u can get to the screws to loosen them you can align the panels accordingly ..as with the hood there are 4 screws that hold it to the hinges and can be ajusted when screws are loosend     good luck <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||286SE'S||06-30-2000||06:41 PM||||With regard to door panels lining up correctly, it may just be that the hinge pins are worn and the door is sagging. One of my cars, the daily driver has the drivers door down by about a 1/4 inch. I can pull it up and it aligns perfect. Worth the time to check this first.<BR>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
